This file records third-party works that gym-tracker depends on, cites, or
displays, and the terms under which it does so.


================================================================================
1. Instructional videos
================================================================================

gym-tracker links exercises to instructional videos, primarily from the YouTube
channel "Jeff Nippard" (https://www.youtube.com/@JeffNippard).

- Videos are shown through YouTube's official embedded player (IFrame API).
- Video files are never downloaded, copied, re-hosted, or redistributed by
  gym-tracker.
- All videos remain the copyright of their respective creators. Embedding
  respects each creator's YouTube embedding settings.
- The exercise-to-video mapping is a hand-curated editorial selection.


================================================================================
2. Scientific literature
================================================================================

Training guidance and the estimated one-rep-max feature are informed by
peer-reviewed research and professional position stands. These works are cited
under normal academic practice. gym-tracker does not reproduce their text,
figures, or tables; full texts remain with their publishers.

The current citation list is maintained in app/references/catalog.py and shown
in-app at /references. Every DOI in that list was verified against the Crossref
API before being committed.

AI-generated exercise guides are original text. The relevant works from the
catalog are attached as "further reading", never paraphrased from source
transcripts or article text. The system prompt forbids the model from naming
any person, brand, book, website, or video and from copying phrasing. Every
guide is shown with an "AI-generated, educational, not coaching or medical
advice" disclaimer. Generation is opt-in per deployment via LLM_PROVIDER and
is off by default.


